  "question": {
    "text": "An electron in an excited state of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ion has angular momentum <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> . The de Broglie wavelength of the electron in this state is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> (where <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is the Bohr radius). The value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
